  "description_html": "Diagram of the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hip&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Hip (page does not exist)\">hipbones</a> ( <i>Ilion</i>, <i>Pubis</i> and <i>Isquion</i> ) in different types of <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Dinosaurs\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dinosaurs\">dinosaurs</a> within the superfamily <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Therizinosauroidea\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Therizinosauroidea\">Therizinosauroidea</a>. The genera is assorted after their calculated age. Very typical for Therizinosauroids is their hips with a pubic pointing backward and fused with the <i>Isquion</i>. Since paleontologists belive the Therizinosauroids evolved from agile predators, the pubic is belived to have reshaped , so the animals could squat to rest when feeding from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tree\" title=\"Tree\">trees</a>. \n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ul><li>The hips are based on information found at <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://the_dinosauria.tripod.com/therizinosaurs.html\">[1]</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://paleontologia.xooit.com/t237-Les-Therizinosaures-et-les-Oviraptorosaures.htm\">[2]</a> (<i>Alxasaurus</i>), <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.dinoweb.narod.ru/TherizinosauriaAlvarezsauria.htm\">[3]</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.dinoweb.narod.ru/nanschiungosaurus.brevispinus1.gif\">[4]</a> (<i>Nanschiungosaurus</i>) and <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.dinocasts.com/prod_productDetails.asp?ProductId=697\">[5]</a> (<i>Alaxasaurus</i>).</li></ul>",
